Cell["\<\
 The checks include t=0, physical bounds or CP/TP, batched versus single-time \
endpoints, and full-chain MatrixExp references at first/middle/last times for \
L<=6, built from regimeHamiltonian. These test the evolution/partial-trace \
pipeline, not independent Hamiltonian assembly. Above L=6 that expensive \
reference is explicitly marked SkippedAboveL. Setup audits check invariant \
blocks before any ED. Negative grand sums within roundoff are retained and \
their rugosity is marked invalid, never clipped. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f3ed1ba-322b-4a4a-80d2-10052da35954"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
 4.A.5 Optional infinite-time values and sampled-window rugosity \
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7a6b5b67-f27e-0347-a25f-973e1e9077bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"qstAInfiniteTime", "=", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"TrueQ", "[", "qstAComputeInfiniteTime", "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"qstAverageState", "[", 
          RowBox[{"qstAEngine", ",", "#"}], "]"}], "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        "qstAClusterTolerances"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<NotRequested\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
    "\n", 
    RowBox[{"qstAWindowR", "=", 
     RowBox[{"qstWindowMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"qstARecords", ",", "\"\<RugosityAB\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"qstAInfiniteTime", ",", "qstAWindowR"}], "}"}]}], "\n", ")"}], 
  ";"}]], "Code",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001120893705662*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[202]:=",ExpressionUUID->"21b66c2e-652b-d04f-a0f8-c68ff0d352cf"],

Cell["\<\
 Energy clusters include all evolved sectors together (ZZ: all four edge \
configurations), preserving coherences within each degenerate cluster. \
Compare the results at all cluster tolerances. The sampled-window rugosity \
uses trapezoidal integration in physical time, including on a logarithmic \
grid. A sampled zero makes this estimate \
Missing[SingularSamplesRequireQuadrature], because an isolated logarithmic \
singularity need not have an infinite integral. It is never replaced by the \
rugosity of an averaged state. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d1cc330-71aa-5d47-b47e-3cfc22444006"]
}, Closed]],

